# secprop-methods.ttl — the sparq-zk PER-METHOD security-properties annotation graph.
#
# [OPUS-4.8] sq-bevd3 (Phase 3; epic sq-0dksu; design record
# research/security-properties-ontology-design.md §5a). 🤖 SPARQ agent —
# security-properties ontology. Written while Fable unavailable; flag for re-review
# when Fable returns.
#
# WHAT THIS IS. The machine-readable form of the per-method security-posture table in
# research/zk-configurable-commitment-security.md §4. It is a STATIC annotation graph
# keyed on the `zk:` commitment-method (`zk:scheme`) and signature-suite
# (`zk:cryptosuite`) IRIs that crates/sparq-zk/src/registry.rs already records per
# credential, using the `secx:` extension vocabulary
# (crates/sparq-trust/ontologies/zkp-sparql/secprop-ext.ttl, behind sparq-trust's
# `secprop-vocab` feature). One annotation block per method IRI: each
# `secx:hasProperty` is a reified (property, level, assurance, audit-status,
# assumption, scope) claim.
#
# WHAT IT IS NOT. It RECORDS claims + their epistemic basis; it is NOT a proof of any
# property. sparq's whole ZK estate is research-grade and NOT externally audited (bead
# sq-qhy4, P0; CR-G1 of compliance/cryptoreview/gap-register.md).
#
# THREE HONESTY RULES (design §5a; enforced by the over-claim guards in
# crates/sparq-zk/src/secprop.rs, which parse this file):
#   1. NEGATIVE properties are `secx:Proven`; POSITIVE privacy/soundness properties
#      are `secx:Claimed` + `secx:ExternalSignOffPending`. "PQ-forgeable" and
#      "Replayable" are SETTLED facts about the construction (a discrete-log signature
#      is Shor-broken; no nullifier primitive exists), so they are Proven. Every
#      positive ZK / soundness / unlinkability / hiding / binding claim about the sparq
#      estate stays Claimed until the external sign-off (sq-qhy4). The only `Proven`
#      rows are conservative / negative ones — the privacy-claims gate, encoded in data.
#   2. SOURCE-cryptosuite properties do NOT transfer to the QUERY proof. A property of
#      a source credential's signature suite carries `secx:scope secx:SourceLayerOnly`;
#      the admissibility ruleset (Phase 2/5) refuses to let it satisfy a query-proof
#      constraint (`zk:sourceCryptosuite` is provenance, not an in-proof property —
#      design §5.3). Omitting `secx:scope` means `secx:QueryProofLayer` (the default).
#   3. COMPLETENESS. Every PRODUCTION-SELECTABLE `zk:scheme`
#      (`commit::CommitmentMethod::is_production_selectable()` == true) has an
#      annotation block — the machine-readable analogue of the "every circuit has a
#      gate-count baseline" gate. The research dial `value-only` is OFF-by-default
#      (compiled out unless the `commitment-value-only` feature is on) and is NOT
#      production-selectable, so it is deliberately NOT a subject here; its least-safe
#      posture is recorded in prose (security write-up §4.3) and surfaced by the Rust
#      `secprop` module's `value_only_posture()` rather than as a static graph block,
#      so the completeness guard keys cleanly on the production set.

@prefix zk:      <https://sparq.dev/ns/zk#> .
@prefix secx:    <https://w3id.org/zkp-sparql/sec-prop#> .
@prefix sig-impl: <https://w3id.org/zkp-sparql/sig-impl#> .
@prefix rdfs:    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .

# ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# (i) zk:poseidon2-rdfc10-v1 — the `string-canonical` method.
# The conservative DEFAULT and the only commitment method implemented end-to-end
# today (security write-up §4.1). Its leaf is a single blake3-token preimage, so
# value↔lexical agreement (INV-VL), term identity, and in-range/single-encoding are
# all machine-enforced in-circuit against an arbitrary committer — but still under
# the unaudited-estate caveat (Claimed + ExternalSignOffPending), NOT Proven.
# Production-selectable.
# ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

zk:poseidon2-rdfc10-v1
  secx:hasProperty
    # positive — Claimed (the in-circuit knowledge-soundness claim; unaudited)
    [ secx:property secx:ZeroKnowledgeType ; secx:level secx:ComputationalZK ;
      secx:assurance secx:Claimed ; secx:auditStatus secx:ExternalSignOffPending ;
      secx:auditEvidence <https://github.com/sparq-org/sparq/blob/main/compliance/cryptoreview/gap-register.md> ] ,
    [ secx:property secx:Soundness ; secx:level secx:KnowledgeSound ;
      secx:assurance secx:Claimed ; secx:auditStatus secx:ExternalSignOffPending ;
      secx:auditEvidence <https://github.com/sparq-org/sparq/blob/main/compliance/cryptoreview/gap-register.md> ] ,
    [ secx:property secx:Completeness ; secx:level secx:Complete ;
      secx:assurance secx:Claimed ; secx:auditStatus secx:ExternalSignOffPending ] ,
    [ secx:property secx:UnlinkabilityScope ; secx:level secx:PerPresentation ;
      secx:assurance secx:Claimed ; secx:auditStatus secx:ExternalSignOffPending ] ,
    [ secx:property secx:Anonymity ; secx:level secx:Identified ;
      secx:assurance secx:Claimed ; secx:auditStatus secx:ExternalSignOffPending ] ,
    [ secx:property secx:Setup ; secx:level secx:Transparent ;
      secx:assurance secx:Claimed ; secx:auditStatus secx:ExternalSignOffPending ] ,
    [ secx:property secx:Interactivity ; secx:level secx:NonInteractive ;
      secx:assurance secx:Claimed ; secx:auditStatus secx:ExternalSignOffPending ] ,
    # negative — Proven (settled facts about the construction; NOT a positive claim)
    [ secx:property secx:PostQuantumForgery ; secx:level secx:PQForgeable ;
      secx:assurance secx:Proven ;
      sig-impl:justification "the issuer signature is discrete-log (Schnorr over Baby-JubJub) and recoverable by a CRQC; PQ-forgeable is a settled NEGATIVE result"@en-GB ] ,
    [ secx:property secx:SingleUse ; secx:level secx:Replayable ;
      secx:assurance secx:Proven ;
      sig-impl:justification "no nullifier / anti-replay primitive exists in the estate (CR-G6 / trust-graph §5.3(3)); Replayable is a settled NEGATIVE result"@en-GB ] .

# ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# (iii) zk:poseidon2-dualleaf-v1 — the `dual-leaf` method.
# The value-optimised method for new issuance (#769). Config-only today (the leaf /
# circuit are unbuilt, sq-j506). Production-selectable, BUT selecting it accepts the
# documented INV-VL DOWNGRADE: value↔lexical agreement is no longer machine-enforced
# — it rests on the `secx:IssuerHonesty` assumption (CR-G8 / sq-qhy4). The downgrade
# is recorded as a property assertion, not hidden. `is_production_selectable()` true
# means ONLY "not a research dial" — NOT an audit / soundness claim.
# ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

zk:poseidon2-dualleaf-v1
  secx:hasProperty
    [ secx:property secx:ZeroKnowledgeType ; secx:level secx:ComputationalZK ;
      secx:assurance secx:Claimed ; secx:auditStatus secx:ExternalSignOffPending ] ,
    # the headline INV-VL downgrade: soundness of the value lane is CONDITIONAL on
    # issuer honesty — a positive property, so still Claimed (never Proven), and it
    # carries the assumption explicitly.
    [ secx:property secx:Soundness ; secx:level secx:KnowledgeSound ;
      secx:assurance secx:Claimed ; secx:auditStatus secx:ExternalSignOffPending ;
      secx:assumption secx:IssuerHonesty ;
      secx:auditEvidence <https://github.com/sparq-org/sparq/blob/main/compliance/cryptoreview/gap-register.md> ] ,
    [ secx:property secx:Completeness ; secx:level secx:Complete ;
      secx:assurance secx:Claimed ; secx:auditStatus secx:ExternalSignOffPending ] ,
    [ secx:property secx:UnlinkabilityScope ; secx:level secx:PerPresentation ;
      secx:assurance secx:Claimed ; secx:auditStatus secx:ExternalSignOffPending ] ,
    [ secx:property secx:Anonymity ; secx:level secx:Identified ;
      secx:assurance secx:Claimed ; secx:auditStatus secx:ExternalSignOffPending ] ,
    [ secx:property secx:Setup ; secx:level secx:Transparent ;
      secx:assurance secx:Claimed ; secx:auditStatus secx:ExternalSignOffPending ] ,
    [ secx:property secx:Interactivity ; secx:level secx:NonInteractive ;
      secx:assurance secx:Claimed ; secx:auditStatus secx:ExternalSignOffPending ] ,
    # negative — Proven
    [ secx:property secx:PostQuantumForgery ; secx:level secx:PQForgeable ;
      secx:assurance secx:Proven ;
      sig-impl:justification "discrete-log issuer signature; PQ-forgeable is a settled NEGATIVE result"@en-GB ] ,
    [ secx:property secx:SingleUse ; secx:level secx:Replayable ;
      secx:assurance secx:Proven ;
      sig-impl:justification "no nullifier primitive; Replayable is a settled NEGATIVE result"@en-GB ] .

# ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# zk:poseidon2-schnorr-v1 — the `zk:cryptosuite` (the issuer SIGNATURE suite).
# Schnorr over Baby-JubJub with a Poseidon2 challenge (sig::SignatureScheme). This is
# the QUERY-PROOF-layer signature sparq itself verifies (NOT a source-credential
# cryptosuite), so its annotations are default scope (QueryProofLayer). PQ-forgeable
# and Replayable are the settled NEGATIVES; the binding-to-an-issuer-key property is a
# positive Claimed under the unaudited estate.
# ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

zk:poseidon2-schnorr-v1
  secx:hasProperty
    [ secx:property secx:Soundness ; secx:level secx:Sound ;
      secx:assurance secx:Claimed ; secx:auditStatus secx:ExternalSignOffPending ;
      secx:assumption secx:DiscreteLog ;
      secx:auditEvidence <https://github.com/sparq-org/sparq/blob/main/compliance/cryptoreview/gap-register.md> ] ,
    [ secx:property secx:PostQuantumForgery ; secx:level secx:PQForgeable ;
      secx:assurance secx:Proven ;
      sig-impl:justification "Schnorr over Baby-JubJub is discrete-log; recoverable by a CRQC — a settled NEGATIVE result, matching the vendored sig-impl: PostQuantumForgery verdict for a DL signature"@en-GB ] ,
    [ secx:property secx:SignatureTypeLeakage ; secx:level secx:SchemeRevealed ;
      secx:assurance secx:Proven ;
      sig-impl:justification "the cryptosuite IRI is recorded in the clear on the registry entry; the scheme is not hidden — a settled NEGATIVE"@en-GB ] .

# ─── ILLUSTRATIVE source-layer-only marker (NOT a sparq production method) ────
# sparq does NOT currently ingest BBS-signed source credentials, but the §5a
# non-transfer rule must be EXPRESSIBLE and TESTABLE. This block annotates the W3C
# Data Integrity `bbs-2023` cryptosuite's cross-show unlinkability with
# `secx:scope secx:SourceLayerOnly` so the over-claim guard's non-transfer check has a
# real subject: a SourceLayerOnly property must NEVER satisfy a query-proof
# constraint. It is provenance about an INPUT credential, not a property of the sparq
# query proof. (When a real VC-cryptosuite ingest bridge lands — sq-9c5e — its
# source-layer properties are annotated this way.) The subject is a sparq-local
# ILLUSTRATIVE IRI (the VC `bbs-2023` cryptosuite id is a STRING in the registry, not
# a resolvable property IRI), named so it is unmistakably a non-production example.
<https://sparq.dev/ns/zk#illustrative-source-bbs-2023>
  rdfs:comment "ILLUSTRATIVE source-layer cryptosuite annotation (a sparq-local example IRI, not the resolvable W3C bbs-2023 id) — sparq does not yet ingest BBS source credentials; present so the source-layer non-transfer guard (§5a rule 2) has a concrete subject."@en-GB ;
  secx:hasProperty
    [ secx:property secx:UnlinkabilityScope ; secx:level secx:CrossPresentation ;
      secx:assurance secx:Claimed ; secx:auditStatus secx:ExternalSignOffPending ;
      secx:scope secx:SourceLayerOnly ] .
